__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Local state — never commit the ledger or the operator's secrets.
#
# The patterns below are wider than they look like they need to be, because
# the narrow versions did not hold. `.env` alone left four `.env.bak-before-*`
# files — each holding live Alpaca keys — untracked but *not ignored*, one
# `git add -A` away from being published. `data/*.db` alone missed
# `mvv.db.bak` and every `mvv.db.before-<change>` snapshot: 1.3 GB of ledger,
# equally committable. Taking a backup before a risky change is the right
# habit; it should not quietly become the way secrets and the trading record
# reach a public repository.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/*.db
data/*.db.*
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
.DS_Store
data/notifications.log
data/metrics.json
data/products.json

# Keep the shipped fixture.
!data/products.sample.json

.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# File Court working directories and the third-party reviewer clone.
uploads/
processed/
logs/
run/
CodeTribunal/

# Trading Edition — the audit vault is this operator's trading record, and
# vendor/ is other people's code. Neither belongs in this repository's history.
vault/
vendor/
data/market/

# Exported dashboards. `trade dashboard` renders your real equity, positions
# and P&L into a file; a local snapshot is yours, not the repository's. The
# CI workflow adds its demo one explicitly with `git add -f`.
dashboard/

# The drop box. A strategy somebody handed you is theirs and stays out of this
# repository — `recruit-watch` should not be a way to commit it by accident.
#
# The fleet ports are different and are listed below. They are first-party:
# our own bots from the sibling repo, translated to the `propose(context)`
# door, and the village is starting to depend on them — a firm whose strategy
# is `bot:bots/veritas_reversion.py` will not run without that file. An
# untracked dependency is not a dependency, it is a copy on one disk, and this
# project has been bitten by that exact shape before (eleven preregs with no
# commits, a ledger fix that sat uncommitted for nine days).
#
# The rule that still holds: anything genuinely foreign gets no line here.
bots/*
!bots/README.md
!bots/example_momentum.py
!bots/example_reversion.yaml
!bots/example_adapter.py
!bots/example_scanner.py

# -- the fleet ports, first-party --------------------------------------------
!bots/atlas.py
!bots/btcc.py
!bots/coinbase.py
!bots/cross_sectional_momentum.py
!bots/fiveway.py
!bots/gatekeeper.py
!bots/keystone.py
!bots/picks_trader.py
!bots/scanner.py
!bots/sentinel.py
!bots/veritas_reversion.py
!bots/wheel.py

# The bridges: they carry a live bot's own output into the signal board rather
# than re-implementing it. See scripts/fleet_sync.py.
!bots/fleet_scanner.py
!bots/fleet_form4.py

# The dossiers that go with them — what each bot is, and what was measured.
!bots/dividend.json
!bots/fomo.json
!bots/form4.json
!bots/kronos_live.json
!bots/trade_journal.json

# The daily village's own state, same reasoning as run/ and logs/ above.
run-daily/
logs-daily/

# Fleet snapshots pulled off Railway volumes by scripts/fleet_sync.py — a cache
# of what the live bots said, re-fetchable at any time and not source.
data/fleet/

# Scouted research candidates — a cache of what is out there, re-fetchable.
# The denominator matters (see scripts/research_scout.py), but the file is data.
data/research/

# The AI queue is live state, not source. Questions and answers are evidence
# and get written up when they matter; the spool itself is transient.
data/ai_queue/

.alpaca_credentials
